## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Changes Made:

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Updated package.json to include the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with the full dependency tree

#### 2. Analytics Integration (src/app/layout.tsx)
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added the `<Analytics />` component to the root layout inside the `<body>` tag
- Followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Directory integration

### Implementation Details:

The implementation follows the latest official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart).

For Next.js projects using the App Directory structure:
- The Analytics component was added to the root layout file (src/app/layout.tsx)
- Placed inside the body element after the children, as recommended
- Uses the Next.js-specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/next`

### Verification:

✅ **Build**: Successfully built the project with no errors
✅ **TypeScript**: Type checking passed
✅ **Linter**: No new linting errors introduced (one pre-existing error in page.tsx was not modified)
✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file properly updated

### Next Steps:

To enable analytics on Vercel:
1. Navigate to Analytics in your Vercel dashboard
2. Select this project and click "Enable"
3. Deploy the app to Vercel

After deployment, analytics will automatically start tracking pageviews and web vitals.

### Files Modified:
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component
